# counters-first-creature at two counters, with Bot1's first creatures entering together: Dragon Fodder makes two Goblin
# tokens at once (CR 101.4, 111.1), and neither entered before the other, so each is the first creature to enter under
# Bot1's control this game and each gets two +1/+1 counters. A creature that enters afterwards (Grizzly Bears, turn 5) gets
# none.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain x2
Dragon Fodder
Grizzly Bears
Forest x2
Mountain x34

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x40

[Variant]
Bot1: emblem Gear test: counters-first-creature, count 2

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Dragon Fodder.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Triggers(Gear test: counters-first-creature, count 2; Gear test: counters-first-creature, count 2)
? Stack.Count = 2
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token#1.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token#2.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
